SUMMARY:Saturday Vibes: 2 Mile Hill
DESCRIPTION:Power up your weekend with Saturday Vibes at Union Summer. \n2 Mile Hill is a band from Barbados that fuses Caribbean vibes with an urban pop sound giving their music an undeniably infectious energy. The band includes Chadd (drums)\, Kris (bass)\, Mahalia (lead vocals) and Russell (lead guitar). Formerly called NexCyx\, a name they dropped in early 2016\, 2 Mile Hill has shared stages with Angie Stone\, Damian Marley\, Erykah Badu\, Sizzla and Wyclef to name a few. In addition to making music\, the band is also the founder of the island’s biggest acoustic music festival\, Mahalia’s Corner. They’ve also racked up awards and accolades at home in Barbados\, and internationally from MTV\, Moët Hennessy Louis Vuitton and RyanSeacrest.com. \nEase into your best summer mood with curated DJ sets spinning feel-good tracks\, setting the perfect tone for sun-soaked hangs. It’s all about great music\, easy energy\, and those spontaneous moments that spark connection and get your day going. \nThis program is in partnership with Barbados Tourism.
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/saturday-vibes-2-mile-hill/
LOCATION:Union\, 65 Front Street West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Union Summer
