SUMMARY:Spotlight on Women: Jennarie
DESCRIPTION:Explore a lineup of women in music with a roster of Toronto’s top female talent. \nMontréal-born and Toronto-based\, Jennarie is an independent artist blending pop\, R&B\, and jazz into a sound that is both soulful and deeply personal. Her songwriting is rooted in emotional honesty and lived experience\, creating music that resonates through vulnerability\, connection\, and self-expression. \nAs a proudly queer\, plus-size\, and neurodivergent artist\, Jennarie uses her music to celebrate underrepresented voices while exploring themes of self-love\, body liberation\, identity\, and personal agency. Her distinctive vocals and thoughtful storytelling have helped her carve out a unique space within Canada’s contemporary music landscape. \nThis program is in partnership with City Hall Live\, a City of Toronto program that creates paid opportunities for local bands and provides accessible live music experiences for residents and visitors.
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/spotlight-on-women-jennarie/
LOCATION:Union\, 65 Front Street West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Union Summer
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontounion.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/d469fcaf-2f5b-42a4-b4d1-472215014087-scaled.jpg
