SUMMARY:Global Music Nights: Kazdoura
DESCRIPTION:Let’s go global! Union Summer’s Global Music Nights\, in collaboration with Small World Music\, bring the world to the waterfront with a vibrant roster of local\, national\, and international artists. \nFor more than two decades\, Small World Music has championed cultural diversity across the GTA—and now that spirit comes alive on our stage. Experience an unforgettable mix of sounds\, rhythms\, and traditions as the patio transforms into a celebration of global talent\, connection\, and discovery. \nKazdoura—meaning “to stroll” in Levantine Arabic—embodies the spirit of exploration\, nostalgia\, and groove. Founded in Toronto by Syrian vocalist Leen Hamo and Lebanese multi-instrumentalist John Abou Chacra\, the JUNO Award-winning duo blends modern and traditional Arabic music with elements of psychedelia\, funk\, and soul. \nKnown for their vintage psych-soul atmosphere\, Kazdoura creates immersive musical experiences where ethereal vocals meet lush\, hypnotic arrangements. Their unique sound bridges cultures and generations\, offering a fresh perspective on Arabic musical traditions. \nThis program is in partnership with Small World Music.
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/global-music-nights-kazdoura/
LOCATION:Union\, 65 Front Street West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Union Summer
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontounion.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/5c63dfa7-bb82-4c7e-83f3-337cbb723178-scaled.jpg
