SUMMARY:Indigenous Spotlight Series: KIMIWVN
DESCRIPTION:Our Indigenous Spotlight Series highlights top contemporary Indigenous music artists on the scene\, in partnership with Meriläinen Müsic Inc. \nMeriläinen Müsic Inc.\, founded by Marc and Laura Meriläinen\, is a majority Indigenous owned full-service record label providing professional music industry services to emerging and established artists. Meriläinen Müsic Inc. is committed to advancing and promoting the careers and opportunities within the music industry for all artists while also specializing in serving the Indigenous Artist community. \n  \nKIMIWVN based in Toronto\, Canada is an Ojicree DJ and producer carving out a distinct space in electronic and house music. Her sound blends ethereal melodies\, deep basslines\, and\npercussive club energy\, moving fluidly between house\, R&B\, pop\, and nostalgic 80s influences. Since her 2021 debut at Lee’s Palace\, she has been refining her craft with emotionally driven\,\ngenre-blurring sets that feel intimate and immersive. Rooted in purpose\, KIMIWVN uses her platform to uplift Indigenous girls and women while continuing to evolve sonically and visually in\na lane entirely her own.
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/indigenous-spotlight-series-kimiwvn/
LOCATION:Union\, 65 Front Street West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Union Summer
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontounion.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/August-3-2026-DJ-Kimiwvn-Promo-Pic-1-scaled.jpeg
